      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T18:01:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A potential short-term solution is to add another property to \"intel,ap-pwrseq-gpio\" that specifies the pin should be asserted at init time.\n\nLonger term, I think I\u0027d like to see an AP chipset node that specify the power signals needed by the AP.\n```\nadl-pwrs {\n    compatible \u003d \"intel,adl\";\n    rsmrst-pwrgd \u003d \u003c\u0026platform_rsmrst_pwrgd\u003e;\n    rsmrst \u003d \u003c\u0026pwr_ec_pch_rsmrst_odl\u003e;\n    slp-s0 \u003d \u003c\u0026pwr_slp_s0_l\u003e;\n    slp_s5 \u003d \u003c\u0026vw_slp_s5_l\u003e;\n    ...\n};\n```\n\nThis could eliminate the need to set the \"enum-name\" on the signal definition.  The chipset driver also knows which signals should be asserted (RSMRST, SYS_RST), so the board wouldn\u0027t have to do this.",
      "parentUuid": "423864cc_20e1561b",
      "revId": "17079caf116a1c7c42a703b821814f7439f0e9ba",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
